  invariant working-set identity and reviewed version remain distinct from title, ordering, filter and inspector focus; changed or removed generic rows drop stale selections atomically
  invariant Source Review explicitly preserves its selected earlier input when later readback changes; selecting the replacement requires removing the earlier selection and source identity includes title, address, native subject, retained text, rights, receipt and publication date
  invariant the shared renderer mounts at most its page size, default fifty rows, from at most one thousand loaded objects; filtered bulk selection respects the consumer selection bound before changing any selection
  invariant resizable panes preserve existing DOM and support pointer capture, Arrow, Home and End controls with narrow-view stacking; tabs use explicit focus and manual activation over the same panel elements
  invariant narrow collections show one focused detail view; returning restores the inspected row and its page without changing selected identities, and leaving details cancels their pending work
  invariant a read-only parent collection cannot hide a nested picker selection or control its detail navigation; layout selectors apply to each collection's own list and inspector
  invariant object navigation focuses the current heading, row removal returns focus to search, and a command dialog closing cannot take focus from a control opened by its command
  invariant the command dialog searches caller-provided actions and rechecks their current disabled predicate when selected; the controller creates no permission, effect or automatic mutation
  invariant obsolete asynchronous inspector work is cancelled and its cleanup invoked; removing an inspected object cannot leave its active source content mounted
  invariant native publication recovery, exact receiving-workspace revisions and save admission remain with their existing owners; these presentation changes add no browser database, credentials or provider requests
